{"base_rate":0.7052631578947368,"brier":0.15590842105263156,"bss":0.24996082089552252,"bss_hi":0.33279025468923235,"bss_lo":0.1774210821812774,"chart":{"base":[976.5,63.8],"fp":[161.7,317.9],"lead":"62,298 272,294.2 482,291.7 692,289.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.25 — higher than 38% of cities","fp":"low end -4pp, high end +12pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.7 °C — better than 98% of cities","rel":"promised 40% → rained 24%; promised 100% → rained 91%"},"rel":"315.5,362.3 558.1,205.1 651.6,98 690.7,73"},"country":"MH","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.12147368421052634,"ess":506.76911491960817,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Majuro</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Majuro rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 7 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>91%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(24%), there is still roughly a <b>14%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 760 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMAJURO WBAS AP, 12.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.25, ranked 132 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(86&ndash;156) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>73%</td><td class='num'><b>61%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>84%</td><td class='num'><b>60%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>91%</td><td class='num'><b>82%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>96%</td><td class='num'><b>88%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>91%</b></td><td class='num'>321</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">7 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Majuro</b> <span class=\"muted\">Marshall Islands</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">7 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.25</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>86&ndash;156\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>760 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Majuro &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Majuro\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\